PUBLIC RESPONSE: {C}

The ESA (as amended) imposes two relevant policy obligations on Ontario employers. Both the disconnecting-from-work policy and the electronic-monitoring policy are required only for employers that have 25 or more employees in Ontario on 1 January of the year in question; the policies must then be prepared (or updated) and distributed in accordance with strict timelines.

- Count date: 1 January of each calendar year.
- Distribution rule: a copy must be given to every employee within 30 days of preparation or any revision, and to every new hire within 30 days of hire.

Option C is the only employer that meets the 25-employee threshold on the relevant count date (1 Jan 2022 and again on 1 Jan 2023). It therefore must maintain both policies and must deliver every revision within 30 days. Updating monthly but distributing only quarterly necessarily means some revisions are delivered more than 30 days late, violating the statute. All other employers fall below the threshold on the applicable 1 January date and therefore have no obligation to create or distribute either policy.

Thus C is the sole non-compliant employer as of 2 January 2023.}

